Basic Selenium Alert Questions (Java)
	1. What are the different types of alerts in Selenium?
		○ Simple Alert (with OK button)
		○ Confirmation Alert (OK and Cancel)
		○ Prompt Alert (Textbox + OK/Cancel)
	2. How do you handle a simple alert in Selenium using Java?
Alert alert = driver.switchTo().alert();
alert. Accept();  // Clicks 'OK'
	3. How do you dismiss an alert (click 'Cancel') in Java Selenium?
Alert alert = driver.switchTo().alert();
alert.dismiss();
	4. How do you retrieve the text from an alert box?
Alert alert = driver.switchTo().alert();
String alertText = alert.getText();
System.out.println(alertText);
	5. How do you send input to a prompt alert?
Alert alert = driver.switchTo().alert();
alert.sendKeys("Test Input");
alert.accept();
 Intermediate/Scenario-Based Questions
	6. What exception is thrown if there is no alert present?
		○ NoAlertPresentException
	7. How can you handle an alert that appears after a delay?
WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));
Alert alert = wait.until(ExpectedConditions.alertIsPresent());
alert.accept();
	8. Can Selenium handle browser pop-ups like file downloads?
		○ No, Selenium can't handle OS-level pop-ups like file download dialogs. You need tools like Robot class, AutoIT, or Winium for that.
		
 Advanced/Tricky Alert Questions
	9. How to verify the alert text and decide whether to accept or dismiss it?
Alert alert = driver.switchTo().alert();
String alertMessage = alert.getText();
if(alertMessage.equals("Are you sure?")) {
    alert.accept();
} else {
    alert.dismiss();
}
	10. How do you test JavaScript alerts triggered by a button click?
WebElement alertButton = driver.findElement(By.id("alertButton"));
alertButton.click();
Alert alert = driver.switchTo().alert();
